  "components": [
    {
      "name": "Default Button",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "button",
      "description": "Everyday action; border brightens on hover.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-btn\">Open terminal</button>",
      "css": ".ds-btn { background: var(--panel-2); color: var(--text); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 6px 12px; font: 14px 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; cursor: pointer; } .ds-btn:hover { border-color: #4a5268; } .ds-btn:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; } .ds-btn:disabled { opacity: 0.45; cursor: not-allowed; }"
    },
    {
      "name": "Primary Button",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "button-primary",
      "description": "The one desk-lamp action in a view.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-btn ds-btn-primary\">+ New agent</button>",
      "css": ".ds-btn { background: var(--panel-2); color: var(--text); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 6px 12px; font: 14px 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; cursor: pointer; } .ds-btn:hover { border-color: #4a5268; } .ds-btn:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; } .ds-btn:disabled { opacity: 0.45; cursor: not-allowed; } .ds-btn-primary { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: #1a1a1a; font-weight: 600; } .ds-btn-primary:hover { border-color: #f2d98a; }"
    },
    {
      "name": "Approve / Reject",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "button-good",
      "description": "Tinted state buttons for permission requests.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-row\"><button class=\"ds-btn ds-btn-good\">Approve</button><button class=\"ds-btn ds-btn-bad\">Reject</button></span>",
      "css": ".ds-btn { background: var(--panel-2); color: var(--text); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 6px 12px; font: 14px 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; cursor: pointer; } .ds-btn:hover { border-color: #4a5268; } .ds-btn:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; } .ds-btn:disabled { opacity: 0.45; cursor: not-allowed; } .ds-row { display: flex; gap: 8px; } .ds-btn-good { background: #1f3d28; border-color: #2f6b41; } .ds-btn-good:hover { border-color: #3fbf5f; } .ds-btn-bad { background: #472023; border-color: #7a3036; } .ds-btn-bad:hover { border-color: #ff5c5c; }"
    },
    {
      "name": "Top-bar Tabs",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "tab-active",
      "description": "View switcher; the active tab is a lit window.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-tabs\"><button class=\"ds-tab ds-tab-active\">Office</button><button class=\"ds-tab\">Command Center</button><button class=\"ds-tab\">Projects</button><button class=\"ds-tab\">Diagnostics</button></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-tabs { display: flex; gap: 4px; padding: 8px 14px; background: var(--panel); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); } .ds-tab { background: transparent; border: 1px solid transparent; border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 6px 12px; color: var(--muted); font: 14px 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; cursor: pointer; } .ds-tab:hover { color: var(--text); } .ds-tab:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; } .ds-tab-active { color: var(--text); background: var(--panel-2); border-color: var(--border); }"
    },
    {
      "name": "Text Field",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "input",
      "description": "Sunken Deep Well field with a Dusk Grey label above.",
      "html": "<label class=\"ds-label\">Folder<input class=\"ds-input\" value=\"~/code/agent-office\"></label>",
      "css": ".ds-label { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; font: 13px 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; color: var(--muted); } .ds-input { background: #0c0e13; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 6px 8px; color: var(--text); font: 14px 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; } .ds-input:hover { border-color: #4a5268; } .ds-input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 1px; }"
    },
    {
      "name": "Chip and Status Pill",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "chip",
      "description": "Branch chip and state-colored status pill.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-chip\">main</span> <span class=\"ds-pill\">Needs permission</span>",
      "css": ".ds-chip { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; background: var(--panel-2); color: var(--text); font: 12px 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; } .ds-pill { display: inline-block; border: 1px solid #ff5c5c; color: #ff5c5c; border-radius: 999px; padding: 4px 10px; font: 13px 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; }"
    },
    {
      "name": "KPI Tile",
      "kind": "card",
      "refersTo": "kpi",
      "description": "Command Center count the user acts on.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-kpi\"><span class=\"ds-kpi-value\">2</span><span class=\"ds-kpi-label\">Waiting approvals</span></div>",
      "css": ".ds-kpi { display: flex; flex-direction: column; width: 160px; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 10px 12px; font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; } .ds-kpi-value { font-family: 'Segoe UI Variable Display', 'SF Pro Display', 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.03em; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: var(--warn); } .ds-kpi-label { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); }"
    },
    {
      "name": "Permission Box",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "permission-box",
      "description": "Tinted alarm box holding a permission request.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-perm\"><strong>Claude Code wants to run</strong><code>npm test</code></div>",
      "css": ".ds-perm { display: grid; gap: 6px; border: 1px solid #7a3036; background: #2a1517; border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 10px; color: var(--text); font: 14px 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; } .ds-perm code { font: 12px 'Cascadia Code', Consolas, monospace; }"
    },
    {
      "name": "Notice",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "notice",
      "description": "Amber notice banner and its subtle info variant.",
      "html": "<p class=\"ds-notice\">Codex needs you to trust its hooks: run /hooks.</p><p class=\"ds-notice ds-notice-subtle\">Simulated demo: no real agents.</p>",
      "css": ".ds-notice { background: #2a2412; border: 1px solid #4a3f1c; color: #f2d98a; border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 6px 10px; font: 12px 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 0 0 8px; } .ds-notice-subtle { background: #182031; border-color: #2a3857; color: #a9c1f5; }"
    },
    {
      "name": "Instruction Bubble",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "",
      "description": "Amber-bordered floating bubble over a character for typing an instruction.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-bubble\"><strong>Tell Ada</strong><textarea class=\"ds-bubble-input\" rows=\"2\">Run the tests again</textarea></div>",
      "css": ".ds-bubble { display: grid; gap: 6px; width: 300px; background: rgba(23, 26, 35, 0.98); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 8px 10px; box-shadow: 0 8px 22px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45); color: var(--text); font: 14px 'Segoe UI', system-ui, sans-serif; } .ds-bubble-input { background: #0c0e13; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 6px 8px; color: var(--text); font: inherit; resize: vertical; } .ds-bubble-input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 1px; }"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Night Office",
    "overview": "You are standing outside an office building at night, looking in through the window. Inside, under desk lamps, the employees are working: typing, reading, raising a hand, slumping after an error. That lit pixel-art room is the only warm, colorful, animated thing on screen. Everything around it (the top bar, the agent panel, the Command Center, Diagnostics) is the dark glass and window frame: low-contrast navy-charcoal surfaces, thin borders, quiet grey type, there to frame the room and hand you the controls, never to compete with it.\n\nThe interface is dense and calm, built for someone who glances at it between other work. Color is spent almost entirely on meaning: the amber desk-lamp accent marks the one action that matters and the focused element; green, red, orange and violet mark state. Surfaces are flat and separated by one-pixel borders and tonal steps, not shadows. The pixel world lends the chrome a few deliberate echoes (hard pixel corners on legend glyphs, pixelated icons, a crisp border on the floating instruction bubble), placed sparingly so the frame still reads as frame.\n\nThis is not a SaaS metrics dashboard: no gradients, no glass blur, no decorative charts, no hero numbers for their own sake. A number earns large type only when it is a count the user acts on.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One dark, flat, tonal chrome; one warm, lit pixel world inside it.",
      "Amber is the single accent; every other hue is a state.",
      "Dense 12–14px system type; monospace only for logs, paths and code.",
      "Depth from tonal steps and 1px borders; shadows only for things that float over the office.",
      "Pixel echoes in the chrome are punctual, never a theme applied everywhere."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Lamplight Rule",
        "body": "Light in the office comes from where people work. A lamp lights its own room only, light is stepped (never a smooth gradient), and characters are never dimmed: the night falls on the floor, not on the people.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Desk-Lamp Rule",
        "body": "Amber marks the one primary action in view and the focused element. If two amber buttons appear in the same panel, one of them is wrong.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Meaning Rule",
        "body": "A state color means one thing everywhere: green is healthy or done, red is error or needs-permission, orange is warning or silence, violet is experimental. Never use them for decoration or category coding.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tinted Box Rule",
        "body": "State boxes use the dark tinted surface plus its edge color, never a saturated fill with white text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Neon Pair Rule",
